{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nActions data is GitHub data. Instead of a separate page (key `6`, shipped in v0.7.0), show workflow runs as a third list column of the GitHub page, next to Issues and Pull Requests, with the run's jobs and log in the shared Detail area. One page less, and `gh` detection, disk cache, `o` (open in browser) and search are shared.\n\n```\n┌ Issues ───────┬ Pull Requests ─┬ Workflow Runs ─┐\n│ …             │ …              │ ● CI #191 main │\n├───────────────┴────────────────┴────────────────┤\n│ Detail                                          │\n│  issue → Body / Comments                        │\n│  pr    → Body / Reviews / Comments / Checks     │\n│  run   → Jobs (job → steps tree) │ Log (tail)   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Spec\n\n- GitHub page KDL: add a `runs` pane to `layout` (three list panes on top, default widths 1/3 each, adjustable via `layout`), `tabs \"issues\" \"prs\" \"runs\" \"detail\"`, `bind select=\"runs\" detail=\"detail\"`.\n- `GhDetailContent` gains a `Run` variant; for a run the detail area shows two sub-panes, Jobs (job → steps tree via `core::tree`) and Log (`TailPane`), using the same sub-pane mechanism as the PR detail (Body / Reviews / Comments / Checks). `Enter` on a job or step loads its log; `]` / `[` jump between failed steps.\n- Behaviour carried over from the Actions page: tick refresh while any run is queued / in progress, log polling for running jobs, `o` opens the run in the browser, `/` search.\n- Remove the Actions page: `src/actions/` domain (`client`, `types`, `time`, `log`) and panes move under `src/github/` (e.g. `src/github/actions/…` or `src/github/panes/{runs,jobs,log}.rs`); `page \"actions\"`, `\"6\" \"page:actions\"` and the `actions` entry of `pages` are removed; Worktrees moves to key / slot `6`.\n- A user config that still lists `actions` in `pages` or binds `page:actions` fails fast with a message saying Actions is now part of the GitHub page.\n- Docs: README (Features, view switching, the GitHub View section absorbs the Actions key table), `docs/README.ja.md`, `docs/config.md`; CLAUDE.md architecture line; `tape/demo-github-*.tape` gain the runs column (drop `tape/demo-actions.tape` / `assets/demo-actions.gif` and the `demo:actions` mise task).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Lands in v0.8.0 as \"Actions page folded into the GitHub page\" (v0.7.0 shipped it as a page).\n- Read-only as before: no rerun / cancel.\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-30T08:08:05Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":118,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Fold the Actions page into the GitHub page as a third column"}
